      "title": "[agrifocusafrica.com] Uganda targets 10,000 tractors in five-year mechanization push",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://kagiproxy.com/img/ApfTDFNZe7lncOvjlfxAb23zxlLA6pc5lx4BKLVD-sddVBbQWGSaXVtHS59loOmCxLddxwGxRPPVLPESl4k8cIkKcQ2q-1qmyveADJl3_i5bfm_7SWrWoDKrazqqc4mYZAkfeY8w6uA\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 0.75em;padding:5px 10px;background:#f0f4f8;border-left:3px solid #7b9fc4;border-radius:3px;font-size:0.82em;color:#444;line-height:1.8;\">🎨 🌾 🔧 🌲 🏔️ 🔭 <a href=\"https://zirnhelt.github.io/super-rss-feed/review.html?url=https%3A%2F%2Fagrifocusafrica.com%2F2026%2F10%2F22%2Fuganda-targets-10000-tractors-in-five-year-push-to-modernise-agriculture%2F\" style=\"color:#7b9fc4;text-decoration:none;\">✏️</a></p>\nUganda plans to deploy 10,000 tractors over five years to expand mechanized farming, Agriculture Minister Frank Tumwebaze told Parliament on Oct. 21. The strategy proposes 21 mechanization centers and a cost-sharing model involving the government, commercial farmers and producer groups. Tumwebaze said dependence on manual labor and unpredictable weather constrain productivity, while machinery could help farmers cultivate more land and support value-added production.\n\nKubota and autonomy-software company Agtonomy are extending a pilot to automate orchard work such as spraying, mowing and underplant cultivation. In the United States, drone-treated acreage grew to 16.4 million acres in 2025. Equipment makers have also introduced higher-capacity grain conveyors designed to reduce harvest handling time.",
